  "execution_status": "not_run_in_this_delivery",
  "requirements": "# Winding diameter observer and speed compensation\n\n- **Difficulty:** Hard (hard)\n\n## Requirements\n\n1. Implement FB_RollGeometry using LREAL and PI=3.141592653589793. Fixed values are CoreD=76 mm, MaxD=140 mm and Thickness=0.135 mm. EncoderDelta is a DINT pulse increment in 0..1000000. A 50 mm diameter measuring roller produces 1024 pulses per revolution.\n\n2. On the first legal call or when Reset=TRUE, initialize StoredLength=PI*(InitialD^2-CoreD^2)/(4*Thickness), Diameter=InitialD, MotorRPM=0 and LimitHit=FALSE. Ignore the pulse increment on this call. InitialD must be in [76,140] and is used only for initialization.\n\n3. On other legal calls, deltaL=EncoderDelta*PI*50/1024. Add deltaL when Receiving=TRUE, otherwise subtract it. Clamp StoredLength to [0,Lmax], where Lmax=PI*(MaxD^2-CoreD^2)/(4*Thickness). Set LimitHit only when the unclamped value is strictly outside this interval; reaching a boundary exactly is not a limit hit.\n\n4. Compute Diameter=SQRT(CoreD^2+4*Thickness*StoredLength/PI) from the updated length. Then compute MotorRPM=SpeedMpm*1000*50/(PI*Diameter) and clamp it to [-6000,6000]. SpeedMpm is signed line speed in [-15,15] m/min. Receiving determines material addition or removal independently of the speed sign.\n\n5. Illegal SpeedMpm or EncoderDelta, or illegal InitialD when initializing, sets Error=TRUE, MotorRPM=0 and LimitHit=FALSE while preserving the length and diameter. Before successful initialization, hold StoredLength=0 and Diameter=76. A subsequent legal call may initialize. Legal calls clear Error. All real inputs are finite.\n\n6. Assume constant thickness, tightly packed winding and no slip or elastic extension. Reset establishes a new geometric estimate; it does not represent material consumption. Absolute comparison tolerances are 0.001 mm for length and diameter, and 0.01 RPM for motor speed.\n\n## Interface Definition\n\n| Direction | Variable/Field | Data Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Input | `Reset` | `BOOL` | Reinitialize the geometric estimate. |\n| Input | `InitialD` | `LREAL` | Initial diameter, 76..140 mm; used only at initialization. |\n| Input | `Receiving` | `BOOL` | TRUE adds wound material; FALSE removes it. |\n| Input | `EncoderDelta` | `DINT` | Pulse increment in this call, 0..1000000. |\n| Input | `SpeedMpm` | `LREAL` | Signed line speed, -15..15 m/min. |\n| Output | `StoredLength` | `LREAL` | Material length outside the core, mm. |\n| Output | `Diameter` | `LREAL` | Estimated diameter, mm; 76 before initialization. |\n| Output | `MotorRPM` | `LREAL` | Motor speed setpoint, RPM. |\n| Output | `LimitHit` | `BOOL` | The material-length update was strictly clipped. |\n| Output | `Error` | `BOOL` | Illegal input. |",
  "ltl": {
    "id": "CUSTOM_04",
    "title": "收放卷卷径估算与转速补偿",
    "definitions": "PI=3.141592653589793，CoreD=76，MaxD=140，h=0.135，Lmax=PI*(140^2-76^2)/(4*h)。\n独立观察器初始initialized=FALSE、length=0、diameter=76。init := !pre.initialized OR Reset。\nvalid := -15<=SpeedMpm<=15 AND 0<=EncoderDelta<=1000000 AND (!init OR 76<=InitialD<=140)，输入均有限。\nvalid AND init时length=PI*(InitialD^2-76^2)/(4*h)，diameter=InitialD，rpm=0，hit=FALSE，initialized=TRUE；忽略脉冲。\nvalid AND !init时raw=pre.length+(Receiving?1:-1)*EncoderDelta*PI*50/1024，length=clamp(raw,0,Lmax)，\ndiameter=sqrt(76^2+4*h*length/PI)，rpm=clamp(SpeedMpm*1000*50/(PI*diameter),-6000,6000)，hit=(raw<0 OR raw>Lmax)。\n!valid时length/diameter/initialized保持，rpm=0，hit=FALSE；不是无条件Reset优先于输入校验。\ngeometryMatch表示StoredLength/ Diameter/MotorRPM/LimitHit分别等于上述独立期望。\n长度和直径测试绝对容差0.001mm，RPM为0.01；LTL数学定义精确，测试容差不改变限幅严格边界。",
    "properties": [
      {
        "id": "P01",
        "formula": "G(Error <-> !valid)"
      },
      {
        "id": "P02",
        "formula": "G(geometryMatch)"
      },
      {
        "id": "P03",
        "formula": "G((!valid) -> (MotorRPM=0 & !LimitHit & StoredLength=pre.length & Diameter=pre.diameter))"
      },
      {
        "id": "P04",
        "formula": "G((valid & init) -> (Diameter=InitialD & MotorRPM=0 & !LimitHit))"
      },
      {
        "id": "P05",
        "formula": "G((valid & !init) -> (LimitHit <-> (raw<0 | raw>Lmax)))"
      },
      {
        "id": "P06",
        "formula": "G(0<=StoredLength & StoredLength<=Lmax & 76<=Diameter & Diameter<=140)"
      },
      {
        "id": "P07",
        "formula": "G(-6000<=MotorRPM & MotorRPM<=6000)"
      }
    ],
